# mutgap3_sys_heap_reply_one_past_page: HeapTextureSizeAndAlign (64) with a 16-byte reply at 2 * PAGE - 15: the reply ends one byte into VA page 2. The service maps the reply's pages with the end rounded up, (offset + length + 0x3fff) & ~0x3fff, so both pages are mapped and all 16 bytes land, the last at 2 * PAGE; the map setup's task maps with the same rounding. The blocks setup does not: its lazy map asks the range tracker for the run of pages, which rounds with 0x3ffe (calculate_page_run_unaligned), one page short when the range ends one byte into a page. Only VA page 1 is mapped (one map_memory), and the 16th byte goes to the task block's unmapped page 2: the guest's byte at 2 * PAGE stays 0xee. The bytes around the reply were 0xee. Host values (the size and alignment Metal reports).
